{"type":"message","id":"07c5f426","parentId":"a010c165","timestamp":"2026-02-18T12:55:02.336Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Great! Now I need to consider that the wrapper batch file might need adjustment because `tee` is not a standard Windows command. Let me check if there's an alternative. I could use PowerShell's Tee-Object, but that would require invoking PowerShell from the batch file. Or I could simply redirect to both console and file using a different approach. Actually, in batch files, we can use `>>` to append to a file but that doesn't show on console. But for a service, console output is not really needed because the service runs non-interactively. However, it's useful to have logging. NSSM captures stdout/stderr and can write to log files itself. So maybe I don't need `tee` at all. I could just let NSSM handle logging.\n\nLet's improve: Instead of having the batch file handle logging, I'll configure NSSM to capture the output. NSSM has options for stdout and stderr log files. So the wrapper can simply run the command, and NSSM will capture its output. That's cleaner.\n\nSo I should update the wrapper to not use `tee`. And then configure NSSM to set AppStdout and AppStderr to appropriate log files.\n\nLet me update the wrapper and install script accordingly.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"Let me improve the wrapper to be simpler and rely on NSSM for logging:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_1a03ebdfc72e4a4e86de84b9","name":"edit","arguments":{"file_path":"D:\\workspace\\appDev\\openclaw\\gateway-wrapper.bat","newText":"@echo off\nREM OpenClaw Gateway Service Wrapper\nsetlocal\n\nREM Change to the OpenClaw installation directory (optional if set in NSSM)\ncd /d \"D:\\workspace\\appDev\\openclaw\"\n\nREM Optional: Echo start message to stdout (captured by NSSM)\necho [%date% %time%] Starting OpenClaw gateway...\n\nREM Run the gateway. NSSM will capture stdout/stderr to configured log files.\nnode \"D:\\workspace\\appDev\\openclaw\\openclaw.mjs\" gateway run --bind 0.0.0.0 --port 8080\n\nREM If the gateway exits, return its exit code so NSSM can handle restart.\nexit /b %errorlevel%","oldText":"@echo off\nREM OpenClaw Gateway Service Wrapper\nREM This script launches the OpenClaw gateway and ensures it stays running\n\nsetlocal\n\nREM Change to the OpenClaw installation directory\ncd /d \"D:\\workspace\\appDev\\openclaw\"\n\nREM Log file location\nset LOG_FILE=C:\\OpenClaw\\gateway-service.log\n\nREM Ensure log directory exists\nif not exist \"C:\\OpenClaw\" mkdir \"C:\\OpenClaw\"\n\nREM Run the gateway with logging\necho [%date% %time%] Starting OpenClaw gateway... >> \"%LOG_FILE%\"\n\nREM Use node to run openclaw.mjs with the gateway run command\nnode \"D:\\workspace\\appDev\\openclaw\\openclaw.mjs\" gateway run --bind 0.0.0.0 --port 8080 2>&1 | tee -a \"%LOG_FILE%\"\n\nif errorlevel 1 (\n    echo [%date% %time%] Gateway crashed with exit code %errorlevel%. Restarting in 5 seconds... >> \"%LOG_FILE%\"\n    timeout /t 5 /nobreak >nul\n    goto :start\n)\n\nendlocal"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free","usage":{"input":27431,"output":1051,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":28482,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1771419296064}}
