{"type":"message","id":"b3a6626f","parentId":"97838393","timestamp":"2026-02-18T12:56:11.025Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The file doesn't exist. Maybe the gateway command is in a different location or the source structure is different. I could search for files containing \"gateway run\". But I can't easily do that.\n\nGiven the AGENTS.md snippet earlier: `openclaw gateway run --bind loopback --port 18789 --force`. That seems like a valid command. So the wrapper should include `--bind` and `--port` options. Which port should be used? The default might be 18789 or something else. I need to check the gateway default port.\n\nLet me search in the docs maybe? The AGENTS.md mentioned port 18789. So that might be the default. I'll adjust the wrapper to use 18789 instead of 8080, and bind to 0.0.0.0 or 127.0.0.1. Typically, the gateway binds to localhost only. In the AGENTS.md example it says `--bind loopback`. So that's 127.0.0.1. That means the gateway is only accessible locally. That's typical for a gateway that proxies requests from local bots. But if the user wants remote access, they might change it.\n\nSo I'll update the wrapper to use `--bind 127.0.0.1 --port 18789`. But I'm not 100% sure. I'll look at the openclaw.mjs more thoroughly to see if it prints help. I could try to execute `node openclaw.mjs gateway --help` to see options. But I can't reliably run it.\n\nGiven the constraints, I'll produce a wrapper that uses a configurable port and bind via variables at the top, so it's easy to change.\n\nI'll also note that if the gateway is run via the service, it should use a persistent config file. By default, OpenClaw uses `~/.openclaw/config.json`. That should be fine.\n\nBut wait, there's also a possibility that the gateway needs to be started with `--force` to avoid prompts? The AGENTS.md says `--force`. That might be needed in non-interactive mode to skip confirmations. I'll add `--force` to the wrapper.\n\nLet's update the wrapper accordingly.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"Let's update the wrapper with proper arguments and configurability:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_5bb18015676b4024860cec9f","name":"edit","arguments":{"file_path":"D:\\workspace\\appDev\\openclaw\\gateway-wrapper.bat","newText":"@echo off\nREM OpenClaw Gateway Service Wrapper\nsetlocal\n\nREM Configuration - adjust as needed\nset OPENCLAW_PATH=D:\\workspace\\appDev\\openclaw\nset GATEWAY_PORT=18789\nset GATEWAY_BIND=127.0.0.1\n\nREM Change to the OpenClaw directory\ncd /d \"%OPENCLAW_PATH%\"\n\nREM Echo start message to stdout (captured by NSSM)\necho [%date% %time%] Starting OpenClaw gateway on %GATEWAY_BIND%:%GATEWAY_PORT%...\n\nREM Run the gateway. NSSM will capture stdout/stderr to configured log files.\nnode \"%OPENCLAW_PATH%\\openclaw.mjs\" gateway run --bind %GATEWAY_BIND% --port %GATEWAY_PORT% --force\n\nREM If the gateway exits, return its exit code so NSSM can handle restart.\nexit /b %errorlevel%","oldText":"@echo off\nREM OpenClaw Gateway Service Wrapper\nsetlocal\n\nREM Change to the OpenClaw installation directory (optional if set in NSSM)\ncd /d \"D:\\workspace\\appDev\\openclaw\"\n\nREM Optional: Echo start message to stdout (captured by NSSM)\necho [%date% %time%] Starting OpenClaw gateway...\n\nREM Run the gateway. NSSM will capture stdout/stderr to configured log files.\nnode \"D:\\workspace\\appDev\\openclaw\\openclaw.mjs\" gateway run --bind 0.0.0.0 --port 8080\n\nREM If the gateway exits, return its exit code so NSSM can handle restart.\nexit /b %errorlevel%"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free","usage":{"input":32643,"output":1376,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":34019,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1771419355658}}
{"type":"message","id":"11248a4e","parentId":"b3a6626f","timestamp":"2026-02-18T12:56:11.045Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_5bb18015676b4024860cec9f","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced text in D:\\workspace\\appDev\\openclaw\\gateway-wrapper.bat."}],"details":{"diff":"  1 @echo off\n  2 REM OpenClaw Gateway Service Wrapper\n  3 setlocal\n  4 \n- 5 REM Change to the OpenClaw installation directory (optional if set in NSSM)\n- 6 cd /d \"D:\\workspace\\appDev\\openclaw\"\n+ 5 REM Configuration - adjust as needed\n+ 6 set OPENCLAW_PATH=D:\\workspace\\appDev\\openclaw\n+ 7 set GATEWAY_PORT=18789\n+ 8 set GATEWAY_BIND=127.0.0.1\n  7 \n- 8 REM Optional: Echo start message to stdout (captured by NSSM)\n- 9 echo [%date% %time%] Starting OpenClaw gateway...\n+10 REM Change to the OpenClaw directory\n+11 cd /d \"%OPENCLAW_PATH%\"\n 10 \n+13 REM Echo start message to stdout (captured by NSSM)\n+14 echo [%date% %time%] Starting OpenClaw gateway on %GATEWAY_BIND%:%GATEWAY_PORT%...\n+15 \n 11 REM Run the gateway. NSSM will capture stdout/stderr to configured log files.\n-12 node \"D:\\workspace\\appDev\\openclaw\\openclaw.mjs\" gateway run --bind 0.0.0.0 --port 8080\n+17 node \"%OPENCLAW_PATH%\\openclaw.mjs\" gateway run --bind %GATEWAY_BIND% --port %GATEWAY_PORT% --force\n 13 \n 14 REM If the gateway exits, return its exit code so NSSM can handle restart.\n 15 exit /b %errorlevel%","firstChangedLine":5},"isError":false,"timestamp":1771419371042}}
{"type":"message","id":"20ecf06f","parentId":"11248a4e","timestamp":"2026-02-18T12:56:23.857Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good. Now the wrapper is more configurable. I've set default to port 18789 and bind to 127.0.0.1 as per AGENTS.md suggestion. The user can change these if needed.\n\nNow, I should also consider that the gateway might require the `--reset` or other flags? But `--force` is enough for non-interactive.\n\nNow, the next step is to actually test the sleep/wake cycle. But as a subagent, I might not be able to put the laptop to sleep programmatically. I can provide instructions for manual testing. The task says \"Test: put laptop to sleep, wake, verify gateway is running and WhatsApp reconnects.\" I should include a testing procedure in the documentation. I already added it to SERVICE_SETUP.md. Let me refine that.\n\nAlso, note that the service should be set to \"Automatic (Delayed Start)\"? Not necessary.\n\nNow, one more thing: The service wrapper uses a hardcoded path to openclaw.mjs. If the project is moved, it breaks. But we're setting it to the workspace path. That's fine for development. In production, the openclaw might be installed elsewhere. But the task says \"likely D:\\Software\\codex\\openclaw.mjs or similar\". So I'll add a note that the wrapper's OPENCLAW_PATH should be adjusted accordingly. Also, the install script default uses the workspace path. I'll add parameters to the install script to allow overriding paths.\n\nActually, the install script already has parameters for OpenClawPath. So that's good.\n\nNow, what about the possibility that the gateway wrapper needs to run with elevated privileges? Probably not; it just runs Node. But the service itself will run under the LocalSystem account by default unless changed. That's okay. The service's account should have access to the file system and network. LocalSystem has broad privileges; but we may want to run as a dedicated user. That's an advanced topic; not necessary now.\n\nNow, regarding the power settings: I've provided a script. But I need to be cautious: Changing power settings to never sleep might not be desirable if the laptop runs on battery. I'll note that.\n\nAlso, I could add a scheduled task to wake the computer at a certain time? That's not needed.\n\nNow, the testing: After wake, verify gateway is running and WhatsApp reconnects. How to verify? Check service status, check logs, and perhaps test a WhatsApp message. I'll include that.\n\nNow, I think I've covered all steps. Let me produce a final comprehensive report. But first, maybe I should also create a script to verify the service status and gateway health. That would be helpful.\n\nBut the task says: \"Report back with steps taken and any issues.\" So my final output should include a summary of what I accomplished, any issues encountered, and the final state.\n\nGiven the exec tool limitations, I couldn't actually install the service or test it. But I've created the necessary files and documentation. I'll assume that the main agent or the user will run the scripts. I'll state that the files have been created and provide instructions.\n\nNow, I should also mention that NSSM must be installed separately. I could optionally include a script to download and install NSSM if not present. But that's out of scope; the task says \"Create/verify a Windows Service using NSSM\". So we need NSSM. I'll assume it's installed or will be installed by the user. I could also check for NSSM and provide instructions.\n\nLet me add a pre-check to the install script to verify NSSM is present; it already does that.\n\nNow, what about the \"gateway-wrapper.bat we made\"? Possibly there already exists such a file in D:\\Software\\codex\\gateway-wrapper.bat. But I've created one in the workspace. That's fine.\n\nNow, I should also consider that the gateway might not be the only component; there might be a web UI as well. But the task specifically mentions \"gateway\" and \"WhatsApp reconnects\", so it's about the WhatsApp channel managed by the gateway.\n\nNow, I need to check if there is any existing service for OpenClaw already. Could be that there is already a service that is failing. I could attempt to check existing services. But given the tool limitations, I'll leave that to the user. The install script will remove an existing service with the same name.\n\nNow, the test: The user should put the laptop to sleep and wake. I'll provide instructions. I'll also mention that if the gateway fails to reconnect, they should check the logs for errors and ensure that the WhatsApp channel is properly authenticated and that network connectivity is restored upon wake.\n\nPotential issues:\n- The gateway might crash on wake due to network changes. The auto-restart should handle it.\n- The gateway might take time to reconnect to WhatsApp. That's normal.\n- If using a VPN or proxy, ensure it's re-established after wake.\n- Windows firewall might block the gateway on startup; ensure exception.\n\nNow, I'll produce a final response summarizing everything.\n\nBut before finalizing, let me ensure the install script is correct PowerShell syntax and includes the new logging configuration. I'll read it to verify.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"Let me review the install script:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_0bd557bc232a4ec598e7c6ec","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"D:\\workspace\\appDev\\openclaw\\install-gateway-service.ps1"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free","usage":{"input":33585,"output":2441,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":36026,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1771419371045}}
{"type":"message","id":"b45d3923","parentId":"20ecf06f","timestamp":"2026-02-18T12:56:23.879Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_0bd557bc232a4ec598e7c6ec","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# OpenClaw Gateway Windows Service Installer\n# Run this script as Administrator\n\nparam(\n    [string]$OpenClawPath = \"D:\\workspace\\appDev\\openclaw\",\n    [string]$ServiceName = \"OpenClawGateway\",\n    [string]$NssmPath = \"C:\\Program Files\\nssm\\nssm.exe\"\n)\n\n# Resolve wrapper script path\n$WrapperScript = Join-Path $OpenClawPath \"gateway-wrapper.bat\"\n\n# Validate paths\nif (-not (Test-Path $WrapperScript)) {\n    Write-Error \"Wrapper script not found at $WrapperScript. Please ensure gateway-wrapper.bat exists.\"\n    exit 1\n}\n\nif (-not (Test-Path $NssmPath)) {\n    Write-Error \"NSSM not found at $NssmPath.`nPlease install NSSM from https://nssm.cc/download`nExtract nssm.exe to $NssmPath or update the NssmPath parameter.\"\n    exit 1\n}\n\nWrite-Host \"Installing Windows Service '$ServiceName' for OpenClaw Gateway...\"\nWrite-Host \"Wrapper: $WrapperScript\"\nWrite-Host \"NSSM: $NssmPath\"\n\n# Remove existing service if it exists\n$existing = Get-Service $ServiceName -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue\nif ($existing) {\n    Write-Host \"Stopping and removing existing service...\"\n    Stop-Service $ServiceName -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue\n    & $NssmPath remove $ServiceName confirm 2>$null\n}\n\n# Install the service\nWrite-Host \"Installing service via NSSM...\"\n& $NssmPath install $ServiceName \"`\"$WrapperScript`\"\"\n\n# Configure service startup type\nWrite-Host \"Setting startup type to Automatic...\"\n& $NssmPath set $ServiceName Start SERVICE_AUTO_START\n\n# Configure restart behavior\nWrite-Host \"Configuring restart on failure (delay 5 seconds)...\"\n& $NssmPath set $ServiceName AppRestartDelay 5000\n& $NssmPath set $ServiceName AppExit Default Restart\n\n# Optional: Set shutdown timeout (default is 5000 ms)\nWrite-Host \"Setting shutdown timeout to 5 seconds...\"\n& $NssmPath set $ServiceName AppShutdownTimeout 5000\n\n# Optional: Set working directory (helps with relative paths)\nWrite-Host \"Setting working directory to $OpenClawPath...\"\n& $NssmPath set $ServiceName AppDirectory \"$OpenClawPath\"\n\n# Optional: Set environment variables if needed\n# & $NssmPath set $ServiceName AppEnvironment \"NODE_ENV=production\"\n\n# Configure NSSM logging\nWrite-Host \"Configuring NSSM logging...\"\n$logDir = \"C:\\OpenClaw\\logs\"\nNew-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path $logDir | Out-Null\n& $NssmPath set $ServiceName AppStdout \"$logDir\\gateway-stdout.log\"\n& $NssmPath set $ServiceName AppStderr \"$logDir\\gateway-stderr.log\"\n& $NssmPath set $ServiceName AppRotateFiles 1\n& $NssmPath set $ServiceName AppRotateBytes 1048576\n& $NssmPath set $ServiceName AppRotateOnline 1\n\nWrite-Host \"`nService installed successfully.\"\nWrite-Host \"Starting service...\"\nStart-Service $ServiceName\n\n# Wait a moment and then check status\nStart-Sleep -Seconds 2\n$svc = Get-Service $ServiceName\nWrite-Host \"Service status: $($svc.Status)\"\n\nWrite-Host \"`nVerification:\"\nWrite-Host \"Check logs: C:\\OpenClaw\\logs\\gateway-stdout.log and gateway-stderr.log\"\nWrite-Host \"To stop the service: Stop-Service $ServiceName\"\nWrite-Host \"To uninstall: & `\"$NssmPath`\" remove $ServiceName confirm\"\nWrite-Host \"To view service properties: Get-Service $ServiceName | Format-List *\""}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1771419383877}}
{"type":"message","id":"213d313b","parentId":"b45d3923","timestamp":"2026-02-18T12:56:42.490Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Looks good. It installs, configures restart, sets working directory, and configures logging. It also starts the service. All good.\n\nNow, I should also consider that the gateway may take some time to start. The script waits 2 seconds and then checks status; that might be enough.\n\nNow, the tasks also mention \"Optionally adjust Windows power settings to prevent aggressive sleep while the service is critical, or ensure the service restarts quickly after wake.\" I've created a script for adjusting power settings to prevent sleep entirely, but also note that auto-restart is sufficient. I'll mention both.\n\nNow, what about the \"test: put laptop to sleep, wake, verify gateway is running and WhatsApp reconnects.\" I need to provide specific test steps. I'll include in the documentation.\n\nNow, ensure I haven't missed any critical steps. The task is to \"Ensure OpenClaw gateway stays running when the laptop goes to sleep and wakes.\" The core solution is the Windows service with auto-restart. That should accomplish the goal: even if the gateway crashes during sleep/wake, the service will restart it quickly.\n\nBut what if the gateway doesn't crash but just loses network connectivity? The service won't restart it because it's still running. The gateway itself should handle network reconnection. That's a matter of the gateway's implementation. Typically, OpenClaw's WhatsApp channel will attempt to reconnect when network is back. So that should be fine.\n\nNow, potential issues:\n- NSSM might not be installed. Provide instructions to download and install.\n- Node.js might not be in PATH for the service. Could fix by setting full path to node.exe in the wrapper or setting AppEnvironment PATH.\n- The gateway might fail due to missing config or credentials. Ensure config is set up.\n- Firewall might block the port.\n- The service might not have permission to write logs to C:\\OpenClaw\\logs. The wrapper runs under the service account (LocalSystem by default) which has full access to C:\\. Should be fine.\n- Port 18789 might be in use. The user can change it.\n- The wrapper uses a fixed path to openclaw.mjs. If the project is moved, update.\n\nThese are all documented.\n\nNow, I'll finalize the documentation. I'll also create a quick summary file.\n\nLet me create a quick start guide:","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"Now let's create a quick start guide summarizing the steps:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_cf1d0e5202164a9fbc1da6de","name":"write","arguments":{"content":"# Quick Start: OpenClaw Gateway as Windows Service\n\n## Prerequisites\n- NSSM (Non-Sucking Service Manager) installed. Get it from https://nssm.cc/download\n  Extract `nssm.exe` to `C:\\Program Files\\nssm\\nssm.exe` (or adjust script)\n- Node.js installed and in PATH (or edit wrapper to use full path to node.exe)\n- OpenClaw project built (`dist/entry.js` exists)\n- Gateway configuration already set up (credentials, etc.)\n\n## Step 1: Prepare Wrapper Script\n\nThe `gateway-wrapper.bat` file is provided. Review and edit these variables if needed:\n```\nset OPENCLAW_PATH=D:\\workspace\\appDev\\openclaw\nset GATEWAY_PORT=18789\nset GATEWAY_BIND=127.0.0.1\n```\n\n## Step 2: Install Service\n\nRun PowerShell as **Administrator** and execute:\n\n```powershell\n.\\install-gateway-service.ps1\n```\n\nOptional parameters:\n```powershell\n.\\install-gateway-service.ps1 -OpenClawPath \"D:\\Software\\codex\" -ServiceName \"OpenClawGateway\" -NssmPath \"C:\\nssm.exe\"\n```\n\nThe script will:\n- Remove any existing OpenClawGateway service\n- Install new service using NSSM\n- Configure automatic startup and restart on failure (5s delay)\n- Set working directory\n- Configure log rotation (1 MB, 1 file)\n- Start the service\n\n## Step 3: Verify Service\n\nCheck service status:\n```powershell\nGet-Service OpenClawGateway\n```\n\nView recent logs:\n```powershell\nGet-Content C:\\OpenClaw\\logs\\gateway-stdout.log -Tail 20\nGet-Content C:\\OpenClaw\\logs\\gateway-stderr.log -Tail 20\n```\n\nIf the service failed to start, check the NSSM error output or Windows Event Viewer.\n\n## Step 4: Test Sleep/Wake\n\n1. Ensure the gateway is running and WhatsApp channel is connected (check OpenClaw UI or logs).\n2. Put the laptop to sleep (Start menu > Power > Sleep or close lid).\n3. Wait 10-30 seconds.\n4. Wake the laptop.\n5. Immediately check:\n   - Service status: `Get-Service OpenClawGateway` should be Running.\n   - Logs: Look for gateway restart or continuation.\n   - WhatsApp connectivity: Send a test message to your own number or check the gateway log for \"WhatsApp connected\".\n\nExpected: The service remains running or quickly restarts (within a few seconds). WhatsApp automatically reconnects.\n\nIf the service stopped during sleep, Windows should automatically restart it (since it's set to automatic). NSSM will relaunch the gateway immediately.\n\n## Optional: Adjust Power Settings (Prevent Sleep)\n\nIf you prefer the laptop not to sleep at all (to avoid any interruption), run as Administrator:\n\n```powershell\n.\\adjust-power-settings.ps1\n```\n\nThis sets sleep timeouts to Never and enables wake timers. You can later revert via Power Options control panel.\n\n**Note**: Disabling sleep may reduce battery life on laptops.\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n- **\"node is not recognized\"**: Edit `gateway-wrapper.bat` to use full path to `node.exe`, e.g.:\n  ```\n  \"C:\\Program Files\\nodejs\\node.exe\" \"%OPENCLAW_PATH%\\openclaw.mjs\" gateway run ...\n  ```\n  Or set NSSM environment: `& $NssmPath set $ServiceName AppEnvironment \"PATH=C:\\Program Files\\nodejs;%PATH%\"`\n\n- **Port already in use**: Change `GATEWAY_PORT` in wrapper to an available port and update any clients accordingly.\n\n- **Permission denied on logs**: Ensure `C:\\OpenClaw` and subfolders are writable by the service account (LocalSystem by default). The install script creates them.\n\n- **Gateway fails to start**: Check the stdout and stderr logs for errors. Common issues: missing `dist/entry.js`, configuration not found, or credentials expired.\n\n- **Service does not restart after crash**: Confirm NSSM restart settings: `& $NssmPath open $ServiceName` to open the NSSM GUI and check the \"Shutdown\" and \"Exit\" actions are set to \"Restart\".\n\n- **WhatsApp does not reconnect after wake**: This is a gateway issue. Ensure you have a stable network. The gateway should attempt reconnection automatically. If not, check the WhatsApp channel code for WebSocket/Puppeteer handling of network changes.\n\n## Uninstall\n\n```powershell\nStop-Service OpenClawGateway -Force\n& \"C:\\Program Files\\nssm\\nssm.exe\" remove OpenClawGateway confirm\n```\n\nRemove log files if desired: `Remove-Item -Recurse -Force C:\\OpenClaw`\n\n## Files\n\n- `gateway-wrapper.bat` - Service wrapper that launches the gateway\n- `install-gateway-service.ps1` - Installer script\n- `adjust-power-settings.ps1` - Optional power settings tweaks\n- `SERVICE_SETUP.md` - Detailed documentation\n\n## Support\n\nFor issues specific to NSSM: https://nssm.cc/usage\nFor OpenClaw issues: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw\n","file_path":"D:\\workspace\\appDev\\openclaw\\QUICKSTART.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free","usage":{"input":35644,"output":2284,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":37928,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1771419383880}}
